cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use LOITER-SIM in your research, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
  A formal academic paper is planned for submission concurrent with the v1.0 release (Q3 2028).

title: "LOITER-SIM: A Deterministic Multi-Agent Simulation Engine for Autonomous UAV Swarms"
version: 0.0.1-pre-alpha
date-released: 2026-05-06

authors:
  - family-names: "Schwartz"
    given-names: "Liran M."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"

abstract: >
  LOITER-SIM is an open-source, bitwise-deterministic simulation engine for loitering
  munitions and autonomous UAV swarms. It provides physics-grade 6-DOF rigid body dynamics,
  Berger-Oliger adaptive mesh refinement, a first-class reinforcement learning API
  (Gymnasium-compatible), and physics-based sensor simulation including radar (RCS-based),
  EO/IR, INS/GPS, and electronic warfare effects. The engine is designed for three primary
  use cases: training multi-agent reinforcement learning systems, evaluating human operator
  performance under mass drone attack scenarios, and analyzing counter-UAS tactics in
  GPS-denied, electronically contested environments.

keywords:
  - drone simulation
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - loitering munitions
  - UAV swarms
  - counter-UAS
  - adaptive mesh refinement
  - deterministic simulation
  - autonomous systems
  - C++17
  - Gymnasium

license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: https://github.com/LiranOG/LOITER-SIM

